<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Tutor Engine (see docs/ai/ARCHITECTURE.md) — the authoritative teaching layer, and the only
    component in HeyGanesh allowed to answer the user (DEC-013's suppression in Voice exists precisely
    because this module is the one that will speak).

    It turns one question — plus optional, bounded, already-resolved screen grounding — into one
    explanation string, and nothing else. No actuation of any kind: the P/Invoke surface of this
    assembly is empty because there is none. No clicks, no typing, no UIA writes, no windows, no
    audio, no capture. Describing an action in prose ("click Save") is teaching; performing one is
    not this module's job.

    Dependency-free, like every module before it: zero PackageReference (all types here are BCL),
    and — deliberately — ZERO ProjectReference either. Not ContextOrchestrator (the input is a
    plain-data TutorContext snapshot, not GuidanceResult), not ScreenCapture (the optional visual is
    opaque JPEG bytes the caller cropped from an already-retained frame; this module never decodes,
    never re-captures, and cannot reach the screen), not Voice/ES/Vision/Overlay (siblings stay
    siblings; DEC-008/DEC-009 discipline). The host wires the edges.

    The one external thing that will ever live behind ITutorClient is an academic/teaching LLM —
    a provider decision deliberately NOT made in this change: the seam ships with fakes and recorded
    frames only, so no provider, model, endpoint, or key name is pre-committed (see DEC-015). No
    field in this assembly can carry a credential.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows10.0.22621.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>HeyGanesh.TutorEngine</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>HeyGanesh.TutorEngine</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>